  "term": "self-defeating behavior",
  "definition": "Self-defeating behavior refers to patterns of acting that work against a person’s well-being, such as behaviors shaped by inaccurate or harmful automatic thoughts. In the source context, changing these patterns can help reduce anxiety and worry.",
